module gunbc.expected_value_authority_audit

import std.types { String, NonEmptyStr, Bool, Int, List, list_length }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, declaration_ref_eq }
import gunbc.semantic_conformance { PrimarySemanticAuthority }

// THE PARTITION THIS CARRIER EXISTS TO PUBLISH: for every enrolled v2 test.claim, does its expected
// side come from something OTHER than the implementation under test, or is it a value the same
// evaluator produced from another expression? The second kind is green whenever the evaluator is
// self-consistent, including when it is consistently wrong, so it measures agreement rather than
// conformance. It is not a defect in itself -- a relation between two production calls is a
// perfectly good authority when the RELATION is the authored statement -- and that is exactly why
// the partition has to be published by identity rather than summarized: the two look identical at
// the call site and differ only in what is being claimed.

// WHY THIS IS NOT DERIVED FROM v2.lens.vacuity, RECORDED BEFORE THE FIRST ROW SO IT IS NOT
// DISCOVERED LATER AS A SHORTCUT. That lens owns TestClaimOperandProvenance and VacuityEvidence and
// it is the nearest existing authority, so re-coining an operand-provenance axis here would be the
// duplicate DESIGN section 3 forbids -- but consuming its VERDICT as this partition's answer would
// be the opposite error and the worse one. VacuityEvidence answers "are the two operands the same
// thing arriving twice"; this partition answers "what statement defines the correct value". Those
// are neighbouring propositions, and the classifier makes the gap visible: its EmitVsEval arm
// returns ProvenIndependent UNCONDITIONALLY, on the stated ground that emit and eval are distinct
// execution paths. For vacuity that is defensible -- the operands genuinely did not arrive from one
// place. For semantic authority it is precisely the sentence this lane forbids, because two
// execution paths agreeing is two implementations agreeing, and that is not a definition. Reading
// one verdict as the other is the authority_substitution class in gunbc.recurring_failure_mode: both
// halves check out and only the arrow between them is invented. So there is no constructor below by
// which a vacuity verdict can inhabit an audit row's basis, and no function here converts one.

// The basis on which a row was classified. A row is only as good as the relation that produced it,
// so the basis is carried rather than assumed, and the arms are the two that can actually be
// computed plus the honest absence. There is deliberately no DerivedFromVacuityVerdict arm.
type AuditDerivationBasis
  = DerivedFromReferenceClosure {
      relation_producer: DeclarationRef
    }
  | DerivedFromAuthoredAuthorityBinding {
      binding_producer: DeclarationRef
    }
  | BasisUnavailable { reason: NonEmptyStr }

// INDEPENDENCE IS RELATIVE TO A NAMED IMPLEMENTATION CLOSURE, not an absolute property of a value.
// A literal is independent of the evaluator; a call to a helper that is itself part of the subject's
// closure is not; a call to a DIFFERENT production authority is independent of THIS subject and
// dependent on that one. Carrying the closure the judgment was made against is what keeps the row
// re-interrogable rather than a remembered opinion.
type ExpectedValueOrigin
  = IndependentOfImplementation {
      authority: PrimarySemanticAuthority,
      judged_against_closure: DeclarationRef
    }
  | DerivedThroughEvaluatorUnderTest {
      deriving_producer: DeclarationRef,
      judged_against_closure: DeclarationRef
    }
  | OriginUnmeasured { reason: NonEmptyStr }

type AuditRow {
  claim: DeclarationRef
  origin: ExpectedValueOrigin
  basis: AuditDerivationBasis
}

// THE DENOMINATOR IS STRUCTURAL AND THE TWO ARMS ANSWER OPPOSITELY AT ZERO ROWS, the same move
// gunbc.semantic_conformance CoverageStanding makes and for the same reason: a partition published
// as a bare list is indistinguishable from a partition nobody ran, and a consumer counting rows gets
// the same zero from both. PartitionMeasured additionally carries the producer, the revision and the
// command, so every number in it is re-derivable rather than transcribed.
type AuditPartition
  = PartitionUnmeasured { subject_universe: NonEmptyStr, blocked_on: NonEmptyStr }
  | PartitionMeasured {
      rows: List<AuditRow>,
      subject_universe: NonEmptyStr,
      measured_revision: NonEmptyStr,
      producer: DeclarationRef,
      command: NonEmptyStr
    }

fn partition_is_measured(p: AuditPartition) -> Bool {
  match p {
    PartitionUnmeasured { subject_universe: _, blocked_on: _ } => false
    PartitionMeasured {
      rows: _,
      subject_universe: _,
      measured_revision: _,
      producer: _,
      command: _
    } => true
  }
}

fn origin_is_independent(o: ExpectedValueOrigin) -> Bool {
  match o {
    IndependentOfImplementation { authority: _, judged_against_closure: _ } => true
    DerivedThroughEvaluatorUnderTest { deriving_producer: _, judged_against_closure: _ } => false
    OriginUnmeasured { reason: _ } => false
  }
}

fn origin_is_unmeasured(o: ExpectedValueOrigin) -> Bool {
  match o {
    OriginUnmeasured { reason: _ } => true
    _ => false
  }
}

// A row whose basis is unavailable cannot support ANY origin claim, so a partition carrying one is
// refused rather than counted with the unavailable rows quietly filed under unmeasured. The two are
// different facts: "we measured this and could not tell" is a measurement, "we had no relation to
// measure with" is not, and collapsing them would let an absent instrument read as a surveyed gap.
type AuditRefusalCause
  = RowClaimsOriginWithoutBasis { claim: DeclarationRef }
  | RowDuplicated { claim: DeclarationRef }
  | MeasuredPartitionCarriesNoRows

fn basis_is_available(b: AuditDerivationBasis) -> Bool {
  match b {
    BasisUnavailable { reason: _ } => false
    _ => true
  }
}

fn claim_occurrence_count(rows: List<AuditRow>, claim: DeclarationRef) -> Int {
  fold(rows, init: 0, f: fn(acc, r) {
    if declaration_ref_eq(a: r.claim, b: claim) { acc + 1 } else { acc }
  })
}

// EVERY ARM OF AuditRefusalCause IS PRODUCED HERE, because an arm no producer can reach is a
// decoration that will later be cited as coverage. The duplicate arm is reachable because rows are
// keyed by claim identity and nothing prevents two rows naming one claim; the empty-measured arm is
// reachable because PartitionMeasured is constructible with an empty row list, which is a claim of
// completeness over a universe the producer never enumerated.
fn audit_row_refusal_causes(rows: List<AuditRow>) -> List<AuditRefusalCause> {
  fold(rows, init: [], f: fn(acc, r) {
    if !basis_is_available(b: r.basis) && !origin_is_unmeasured(o: r.origin) {
      concat(acc, [RowClaimsOriginWithoutBasis { claim: r.claim }])
    } else {
      if claim_occurrence_count(rows: rows, claim: r.claim) > 1 {
        concat(acc, [RowDuplicated { claim: r.claim }])
      } else {
        acc
      }
    }
  })
}

fn audit_partition_refusal_causes(p: AuditPartition) -> List<AuditRefusalCause> {
  match p {
    PartitionUnmeasured { subject_universe: _, blocked_on: _ } => []
    PartitionMeasured {
      rows: rows,
      subject_universe: _,
      measured_revision: _,
      producer: _,
      command: _
    } =>
      if list_length(items: rows) == 0 {
        [MeasuredPartitionCarriesNoRows]
      } else {
        audit_row_refusal_causes(rows: rows)
      }
  }
}

fn count_rows_with_origin_independent(rows: List<AuditRow>, want_independent: Bool) -> Int {
  fold(rows, init: 0, f: fn(acc, r) {
    if origin_is_independent(o: r.origin) == want_independent { acc + 1 } else { acc }
  })
}

// THE MEASUREMENT HAS NOT BEEN PERFORMED AND THIS ROW SAYS SO IN THE ONLY WAY THAT STAYS TRUE. The
// lane that owns this carrier is under a model-work-only gate: the reference-closure relation that
// decides independence is a corpus-wide read, and running it now would produce a number ahead of the
// gate that authorizes it. Publishing PartitionUnmeasured is therefore the honest state rather than
// a placeholder -- and it is not the same as publishing an empty measured partition, which is the
// distinction the type above exists to make. BLOCKED_ON NAMES THE CAPABILITY, not an artifact: the
// audit becomes computable when a reference-closure relation can answer, for a named test.claim's
// expected-side expression, whether every producer it reaches lies inside the subject's own
// implementation closure. v2.lens.reference_deps is the nearest existing producer of that relation
// and is named as the starting point rather than as the answer.
data v2_test_claim_expected_value_partition: AuditPartition = PartitionUnmeasured {
  subject_universe: "every enrolled v2 test.claim under src/v2/test/claim" as NonEmptyStr,
  blocked_on: "a reference-closure relation able to decide, for a named test.claim's expected-side expression, whether every producer it reaches lies inside the subject's own implementation closure; v2.lens.reference_deps is the nearest existing producer of that relation. The lane is additionally under a model-work-only gate that forbids corpus-wide measurement until released." as NonEmptyStr,
}

data audit_instrument_substitution_note: String = "WHY THE PARTITION IS UNMEASURED RATHER THAN DERIVED FROM AN INSTRUMENT THAT IS ALREADY RUNNING. v2.lens.vacuity classifies test claims into ProvenDuplicate | ProvenIndependent | Unknown over TestClaimOperandProvenance, and it would have been one join away from a published partition. It answers a NEIGHBOURING PROPOSITION: whether the two operands of a claim are the same value arriving twice. This carrier's proposition is what statement DEFINES the correct value. The gap is visible in one arm: classify_vacuity_evidence_record returns ProvenIndependent unconditionally for EmitVsEval, because emit and eval are distinct execution paths. That is sound for operand duplication and is exactly the forbidden sentence for semantic authority, since two execution paths agreeing is two implementations agreeing. Deriving this partition from that verdict would have been authority substitution -- one authority borrowed to answer for another's, with both halves true and only the arrow invented -- and it would have arrived as a number, which is the form in which it would never have been questioned. NOT A FINDING AGAINST THE VACUITY LENS: no claim is made here that its arm is wrong for its own question, and no edit to it is proposed by this module."
